---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import finishChute from '../assets/photos/finish-chute.jpg';
import swimExit from '../assets/photos/swim-exit.jpg';

// The road here, as splits.
const timeline = [
  { when: 'College', what: 'D1 water polo. Years of cold pools and late-game calf cramps.', color: 'var(--swim)' },
  { when: '2025', what: 'Raced the Chicago Triathlon.', color: 'var(--bike)' },
  { when: 'Sept 2026', what: '70.3 Michigan. Goal: under 5 hours. Result: 5:22:56.', color: 'var(--run)' },
  { when: 'Nov 2026', what: 'Base training starts, with an AI as my coach.', color: 'var(--trans)' },
  { when: '2027', what: 'A couple of 70.3s, including a Michigan rematch. Then my first full Ironman.', color: 'var(--accent)' },
];
---
<Base title="About" description="I'm James, a Chicago frontend developer and former D1 water polo player. I missed my 70.3 goal, so I'm letting AI coach me to a rematch and a first Ironman.">
  <section class="wrap section hero">
    <div class="stack copy">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h1>I missed my goal by 23 minutes.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I’m James. I’m a frontend developer in Chicago, a former D1 water polo player, and an age-group triathlete.
        Split Decisions is how I’m getting those minutes back, in public.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="photo">
      <Image
        src={finishChute}
        alt="James smiling as he runs down the finish chute at Ironman 70.3 Michigan"
        widths={[480, 800, 1200]}
        sizes="(width < 40rem) 100vw, 45vw"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption class="mono">70.3 Michigan · 5:22:56</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <article class="wrap story stack">
    <h2>The race</h2>
    <p>
      At Ironman 70.3 Michigan in September 2026 I was aiming to go under five hours. The swim went the way I hoped:
      I came out of the water 7th in my age group. Then my calves cramped while I was pulling off my wetsuit, and the
      rest of the day was a slow leak. A dropped chain on the bike, a fade over the last miles, two stops on the run. I
      finished in 5:22:56, 46th in my division.
    </p>
    <p>
      Afterward I gave an AI everything I had from the race: my splits, my watch files and my notes from each leg. I
      asked it where the time went. It came back with a breakdown I couldn’t argue with: about 10 minutes on the bike,
      7 on the run and 6 in transitions, nearly all of it tied to cramps I’d been ignoring since my water polo days.
    </p>

    <h2>Why Split Decisions</h2>
    <p>
      A race is a pile of small decisions. How hard to push on the bike, when to eat, whether to stop. Training is the
      same thing stretched over months, and most of us make those calls on feel. A split is the time you get at each
      timing mat. A decision is what you do about it.
    </p>
    <p>
      So I’m letting an AI coach me. Not a canned plan: a coach that works from my real data, explains every change in
      plain language, and tells me straight when I’m skipping sessions or riding my easy days too hard. I’m sharing the
      whole setup in <a href="/guide/">the guide</a>, written so it works for any sport, and I’m posting how it goes
      on <a href="/progress/">my progress page</a> and on YouTube, including the weeks that go badly.
    </p>

    <h2>Where this is going</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {timeline.map((t) => (
        <li style={`--leg: ${t.color}`}>
          <span class="mono when">{t.when}</span>
          <span>{t.what}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <figure class="inline-photo">
      <Image src={swimExit} alt="James running out of the lake after the swim in a wetsuit and green cap" widths={[600, 900]} sizes="(width < 48rem) 100vw, 48rem" />
      <figcaption class="muted">The part that went to plan.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>What I’m not</h2>
    <p>
      I’m not a certified coach, and AI isn’t one either. It’s a tool that’s good at reading data and explaining
      tradeoffs. If something hurts, see a doctor before you ask a chatbot. What I can promise is that I’ll show you
      what actually happens, with real numbers.
    </p>
  </article>

  <div class="wrap section">
    <Signup />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 24rem), 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-l);
      align-items: center;
    }
    .copy { --stack-gap: var(--space-m); }
    .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-muted); }
    .photo { margin: 0; position: relative; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; overflow: hidden; border-radius: var(--radius); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .photo img { inline-size: 100%; block-size: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 72% 30%; }
    .photo figcaption {
      position: absolute;
      inset: auto auto var(--space-s) var(--space-s);
      background: rgb(14 17 22 / 0.85);
      backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
      padding: 0.35em 0.7em;
      border-radius: 6px;
      border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--accent);
      font-size: var(--step--1);
    }

    .story { --stack-gap: var(--space-s); max-inline-size: 44rem; padding-block-end: var(--space-xl); }
    .story h2 { margin-block-start: var(--space-l); }
    .story p { color: var(--ink-muted); }
    .story a { color: var(--ink); }

    .timeline { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0; }
    .timeline li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-s);
      padding: 0.8rem 0 0.8rem 0.9rem;
      border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--leg);
    }
    .timeline li + li { border-block-start: 1px dashed var(--line); }
    .when { color: var(--leg); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: var(--step--1); padding-block-start: 0.15em; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
        .timeline li { animation: slide linear both; animation-timeline: view(); animation-range: entry 0% entry 80%; }
      }
    }
    @keyframes slide { from { opacity: 0; translate: -1rem 0; } }

    .inline-photo { margin: var(--space-m) 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
    /* The swim photo is portrait: keep the top of the frame (my head) whatever the crop. */
    .inline-photo img { inline-size: 100%; block-size: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 12%; border-radius: var(--radius); }
    @media (width < 40rem) { .inline-photo img { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; } }
    .inline-photo figcaption { font-size: var(--step--1); }
  }
</style>
